<title>USA: Vitro SA Q3 net loss vs profit.</title>
<headline>Vitro SA Q3 net loss vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Net loss of	    3,210.8   profit	 163.5</p>
<p>majority interest</p>
<p> Net loss		$3,107.9   profit	$239.9</p>
<p> Net Sales		4,234.3		  4,042.3</p>
<p>	  9 MONTHS</p>
<p> Net loss of	   $3,755.6   profit    $1,296.2</p>
<p>majority interest</p>
<p> Net loss		 3,465.7   profit     1,591.1</p>
<p> Net Sales	     12,311.5		 12,132.9</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are given in pesos unless otherwise indicated and all comparisons are made in constant pesos as of September 30, 1996. The exchange rate used for the financial statements was $7.555 pesos/dollar, the company said.</p>
<p>The results include the assets of Anchor Glass Container Corp, an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary, which Vitro plans to sell to Ball-Foster Glass Container Co for $365 million.</p>
